usage: loop [-h] [--project PROJECT] [--goal GOAL] [--json] [--version]
            {install,goal,approve,queue,list,use,status,next,plan,stage-done,requirements,task,check,verify,note,ask,answer,block,unblock,finish,pause,resume,stop,start,run,dashboard,statusline,roles,notify,telegram-bot,telegram-setup,log,audit,repair,mcp,request,propose,review,migrate-legacy,_job} ...

Loop Engineering 2: autonomous goal loops with verified completion and visible
status.

positional arguments:
  {install,goal,approve,queue,list,use,status,next,plan,stage-done,requirements,task,check,verify,note,ask,answer,block,unblock,finish,pause,resume,stop,start,run,dashboard,statusline,roles,notify,telegram-bot,telegram-setup,log,audit,repair,mcp,request,propose,review,migrate-legacy,_job}
    install             Connect this project to Claude Code / Codex / other
                        agents
    goal                Create a goal (or edit .loop/goals/<id>/goal.json and
                        run `loop approve`)
    approve             Approve the current goal contract (you, the human);
                        --goal <id> for a queued one
    queue               Show or edit the ordered goal queue (the runner
                        continues with approved queued goals)
    list                List goals
    use                 Make a goal the current one
    status              Show status
    next                Show the next assignment
    plan                Add/update tasks from JSON (list of tasks) or one
                        --add
    stage-done          Full pipeline: record the document of a stage (intake,
                        solution, test_design, resources)
    requirements        Full pipeline: record requirements from a JSON list,
                        or show them
    task                start or finish a task
    check               Run checks through the controller
    verify              Controller runs acceptance now and applies the result
    note                Record a note
    ask                 Ask the human (or request approval)
    answer              Answer an open question
    block               Block the goal for a human
    unblock             Clear a blocker after resolving it
    finish              Submit the final report; the controller verifies
                        acceptance
    pause               Pause the goal
    resume              Resume the goal
    stop                Stop the goal
    start               Start the autonomous runner in the background
    run                 Run the autonomous runner in the foreground
    dashboard           Serve a read-only local status page
    statusline          One status line (Claude Code statusLine command)
    roles               List specialist roles and where each guide comes from
                        (.loop/roles/<role>.md overrides)
    notify              Send a test notification; --progress on|off toggles
                        per-turn progress messages
    telegram-bot        Run the two-way Telegram bot (answer/approve/unblock
                        from the chat); `start` launches it
    telegram-setup      Connect Telegram notifications (asks for the bot token
                        in this terminal)
    log                 Show recent events
    audit               Verify the event hash chain and state integrity
    repair              Accept an inspected external state edit
    mcp                 Run the MCP server on stdio
    request             Submit a new requirement: the planning agent drafts it
                        as a queued goal for your approval
    propose             Run the planning agent: it drafts and queues the next
                        goals for your approval
    review              Record a review verdict yourself (human override)
    migrate-legacy      Migrate a Loop Engineering v1 project and state into
                        this version
    _job                ==SUPPRESS==

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --project PROJECT     Project root (default: search upward from cwd)
  --goal GOAL           Goal id (default: current goal)
  --json                Print JSON
  --version             show program's version number and exit
